Z||000026||jlhuber||11-29-2000||09:01 PM||||--Hey, I'm from Michigan too.  I am in the Air Force currently in New Jersey as you can see to the left margin.  I am planning on getting out of active duty and getting a real (read: better paying) job.  You guys start up a club or something, I'll don't mind driving a bit to join other fiero addicts.  Just tell me when and where.<P>--Pontiaddict, I'm from Midland county (Edenville/Hope area to be exact).  I went to high school with a girl who drove a gold '85 SE.  Man she was a hot one, the girl I mean, course the car was nice too.  You know, to tell you the truth it could have been a GT.  I never did get a good look at the car for I was always ...uh ...distracted by the *scenery*. Out of curiosity, what were the cosmetic differences in the '85 SE &'85 GT?  Anyways, as it happens, I bought my '86 GT from the guy who was her boyfriend at the time.  I sold that GT about two months ago and I am going this saturday to look at another one.  If everything goes as I hope, I'll be driving my 2nd Fiero on Monday.  WOOHOO!  I can't wait for these withdrawl symptoms to stop. ||||reg||14
Z||000027||FieroMaster88||11-29-2000||11:02 PM||||OK, Heres the scoop.  Seeing how there are so many of us from South West Michigan, I guess we should start a club!  Would be awesome!  Anyone is welcome.  The "Ohio boys" are welcome too.  Archie, you too.  If you have a Fiero project currently going on, if you dont have a fiero but you are getting one, whatever, YOU CAN JOIN!  I just want a place where people with a common interest can get together and share information, and a place to make friends and help one another.  I would make a website, but I am not very good at it and dont have a lot of time i can devote to it, so if someone else could, let me know.  <P>James||||reg||1
